			<item>
				<title>002 Independent Researcher Manifesto: The Right to Structure</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/independent-researcher-manifesto/002-the-right-to-structure/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2026 11:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/independent-researcher-manifesto/002-the-right-to-structure/</guid>
				<description>Moving beyond interpretation, this manifesto explores structure as invisible power, legitimacy without permission, protocol-centered value creation, and the architecture of sovereign systems.</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>004 Independent Researcher Manifesto: The Right to Simplicity</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/independent-researcher-manifesto/004-the-right-to-simplicity/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/independent-researcher-manifesto/004-the-right-to-simplicity/</guid>
				<description>Simplicity is not the absence of complexity but its highest integrated form. Any system ultimately exists to protect the fundamental conditions of life: home, childhood, peace, safety, and human dignity.</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>006 Independent Researcher Manifesto: The Right to Human Outcomes</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/independent-researcher-manifesto/006-the-right-to-human-outcomes/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/independent-researcher-manifesto/006-the-right-to-human-outcomes/</guid>
				<description>Systems, models, and institutions are instruments of navigation. Their value is determined by whether they help people live, love, create, return home, and build the future.</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>010 Coordinates of the Heart. Vector Navigation and the Ethics of Inner Honesty</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/core-recalibration/010-2026-coordinates-of-the-heart-vector-navigation-and-the-ethics-of-inner-honesty/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 30 May 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/core-recalibration/010-2026-coordinates-of-the-heart-vector-navigation-and-the-ethics-of-inner-honesty/</guid>
				<description>The heart answers &amp;lsquo;Where?&amp;rsquo;. The mind answers &amp;lsquo;How?&amp;rsquo;. Core Recalibration begins when absence of energy is recognized as a system signal rather than a personal failure.</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>012 The Architecture of Meaning Environments. The Vitruvian Triad of Sovereign Thinking</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/core-recalibration/012-2026-the-architecture-of-meaning-environments-the-vitruvian-triad-of-sovereign-thinking/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 31 May 2026 23:00:00 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/en/docs/core-recalibration/012-2026-the-architecture-of-meaning-environments-the-vitruvian-triad-of-sovereign-thinking/</guid>
				<description>Construction creates objects. Architecture designs the environments in which those objects become possible. This article marks the final stage of Core Recalibration and introduces the architecture of meaning environments as a sovereign systems-thinking discipline.</description>
			</item>
			<item>
